  "caveats": [
    "Private typed adoption and fencing. Unknown native raw prefixes still fail; exact root/images, ancestors, pending votes, floors and original install/fencing rules remain required.",
    "Four actual public-bootstrap profiles drive votes and campaigns in the test. Six removed-node adoptions use complete authenticated owner copies over loopback TCP. This is not autonomous membership or public READY.",
    "The final two integration suites use the final isolated build. Six unaffected suites passed on its identical production classes in the prior build; that overall prior build failed because the new inspection worker mistakenly requested a governing floor from a removed node. The original failure remains retained.",
    "Thirty-eight crash cases at all 19 adoption boundaries use one actual 4-to-3 EMPTY history. Workers read actual retained source ownership, not caller historical observations. Halt/SIGKILL and lock checks do not establish power-loss durability or the full distributed failure matrix.",
    "Autonomous discovery/election scheduling, native pending-context turnover, learner ADD/REPLACE and joint completion, generalized distributed publication and complete Phase 3 obligations remain open.",
    "No public factory, format, limit, deadline, POM, workflow, V5.2 Runner, paid experiment, push or release change."
  ],
